                      --          --


Create test makefile target for some testsuite/[DONE rsync 2.5.x]

  The 'make check' (and its alias 'make test') target has been present
  for many years.  Running 'make check' builds rsync and runs the test
  suite in the testsuite/ directory via runtests.py.  Protocol
  compatibility variants are available as 'make check29' and
  'make check30'.  An installcheck target also exists to test an
  already-installed rsync binary.

                      --          --

RELATED PROJECTS -----------------------------------------------------

rsyncsh

   Write a small emulation of interactive ftp as a Python program
   that calls rsync.  Commands such as "cd", "ls", "ls *.c" etc map
   fairly directly into rsync commands: it just needs to remember the
   current host, directory and so on.  We can probably even do
   completion of remote filenames.

